                      </tbody></table></div>
                    ) : <p class="muted">Google has not shown the site for any search in these 28 days.</p>}
                  </article>
                  <article class="card wide">
                    <h2>Pages that show up <span class="muted">last 28 days · change in average position vs the 28 days before</span></h2>
                    {sv.pages.length ? (
                      <div class="tablewrap"><table class="tracker search-table"><thead><tr><th>Page</th><th class="num">Impr.</th><th class="num">Clicks</th><th class="num">Avg. position</th><th class="num">Change</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                        {sv.pages.slice(0, 25).map((p: any) => (
                          <tr><td><a href={p.page}>{p.page}</a></td><td class="num">{p.impressions}</td><td class="num">{p.clicks}</td><td class="num">{p.position.toFixed(1)}</td><td class="num"><Fragment set:html={rowChange(p)} /></td></tr>
                        ))}
                      </tbody></table></div>
                    ) : <p class="muted">No page of the site appeared on Google in these 28 days.</p>}
                  </article>
                </div>
              </>
          ) : (
            <div class="card">
              <h2>Google Search Console <span class="muted">not connected yet</span></h2>
              <p class="muted">Connect it once (SETUP.md, section "Search Console data") and this tab shows clicks, impressions, average position, indexed pages, and the queries and pages that bring traffic, refreshed every run.</p>
              <p class="muted">Meanwhile: <a href="https://search.google.com/search-console" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Search Console ↗</a> · <a href="https://www.bing.com/webmasters" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bing Webmaster Tools ↗</a> · IndexNow submits every new story automatically.</p>
